# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment template
#
# THE APPLICATION RUNS WITH NO ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES SET.
#
# Every provider in this codebase is a demo adapter (src/providers/demo). Nothing
# calls a vendor API, so there are no credentials to supply. Copy this file to
# `.env.local` only if you want to pin which client a local dev server serves.
#
# Everything below the first section is COMMENTED OUT and NOT YET IMPLEMENTED.
# Those names are illustrative placeholders showing the shape a future adapter
# would read — no code reads any of them today. Do not treat them as an
# integration contract; the adapter that eventually lands picks its own names.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client selection — the only variable this codebase actually reads
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Read in src/config/active.ts. One deployment serves one client.
#
# Registered slugs (the keys of the registry in src/config/active.ts):
#   template          legacy SiteConfig scaffold; all modules off (marketing only)
#   teen-edge         legacy SiteConfig; booking enabled
#   mentor-academy    legacy SiteConfig; booking + content enabled
#   collective        legacy SiteConfig; community enabled
#   experience-demo   ClientConfig, interactive-experiences preset ("Lantern Rooms")
#
# The four legacy configs are adapted at load by normalizeLegacyConfig(). The
# `content` and `community` modules are foundation-only: they contribute no UI.
#
# Unset falls back to "teen-edge". An unknown slug logs a warning and also falls
# back to "teen-edge" rather than failing the build.

NEXT_PUBLIC_CLIENT=experience-demo


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider credentials — NOT YET IMPLEMENTED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# src/providers/types.ts defines five provider interfaces. Each has exactly one
# implementation today: the demo adapter. src/providers/index.ts THROWS if a
# client's `integrations` block requests any provider other than "demo", so
# setting a variable below does not enable anything — an adapter has to be
# written under src/providers/<vendor>/ first.
#
# See docs/provider-integrations.md for what each production adapter must do.


# --- Auth (AuthProvider) --- NOT YET IMPLEMENTED ---------------------------
# Demo adapter: DemoAuthProvider returns a seeded persona from
# src/data/seed/viewers.ts. There is no sign-in, no session, no authorization.
#
# AUTH_PROVIDER_URL=
# AUTH_PROVIDER_CLIENT_ID=
# AUTH_PROVIDER_CLIENT_SECRET=


# --- Commerce (CommerceProvider) --- NOT YET IMPLEMENTED -------------------
# Demo adapter: DemoCommerceProvider returns `demo_charge_*` / `demo_refund_*` /
# `demo_payout_*` references. No card is charged and no payout is scheduled.
#
# COMMERCE_API_KEY=
# COMMERCE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=


# --- Session / live video (SessionProvider) --- NOT YET IMPLEMENTED --------
# Demo adapter: DemoSessionProvider mints a `demo_room_*` id pointing at the
# in-app shell route and a non-functional placeholder token. No room is created
# on any service and there is no media transport.
#
# SESSION_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# SESSION_PROVIDER_API_SECRET=
# SESSION_PROVIDER_WS_URL=
# TURN_SERVER_URL=
# TURN_SERVER_USERNAME=
# TURN_SERVER_CREDENTIAL=


# --- Media (MediaProvider) --- NOT YET IMPLEMENTED -------------------------
# Demo adapter: DemoMediaProvider maps a sample ref to a local path under
# /public. No CDN, no signing, no remote host.
#
# MEDIA_PROVIDER_TOKEN=
# MEDIA_PLAYBACK_SIGNING_KEY=


# --- Messaging (MessagingProvider) --- NOT YET IMPLEMENTED -----------------
# Demo adapter: DemoMessagingProvider returns { ok: true } and delivers nothing.
# Conversations live in the in-memory repository for the process lifetime.
#
# MESSAGING_PROVIDER_API_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Persistence — NOT YET IMPLEMENTED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# src/data/repositories.ts defines the repository interfaces; the only adapter
# is the in-memory one in src/data/memory. No database dependency has been
# added, so there is no connection string to set.
#
# DATABASE_URL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not environment variables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These are configured per client in `clients/<slug>/…`, not here:
#   integrations.formEndpoint    lead-capture endpoint (POST /api/lead validates
#                                and acknowledges but delivers nowhere)
#   integrations.analytics       { provider, id } — no analytics script is
#                                currently injected by the app
#   integrations.bookingEmbedUrl third-party appointment embed for legacy clients
